     { id: "coev-quilt-writer-glue", claim: "a C1 player can keep their work — the coev banner saves a ONE-lane quilt {kind: 'pong-quilt/coev@v1', genC, sChamp, eChamp, popS, popE, last, ledger} with no classic field able to disagree with the weights (the R56 P3/R59 M1/R63 M2 three-lineage split dead by construction), and the file input routes a coev file back into the C1 lane VERBATIM — the file's populations restore exactly (keeping your work means THIS population, not a re-seeding around the champs; that treatment is the artifact lane's, loadCoev), the classic splice is structurally unreachable for coev files (the classic loader refuses them NAMED by construction), classic slots are byte-untouched by a coev-file load, a coev-shaped file missing load-bearing fields is LOAD/COEV-MALFORMED with zero state change, one Train after the load advances genC by exactly 1 at slider-sized populations, and a champ-less gen-0 file clears the served game (no champ means no serve — a null champNet into live() froze the page, verbatim-repro'd TypeError 'b1', the R49 P1 class, found by this round's own play and fixed in-branch) — FAIL-first on the pre-R67 tip: T1–T3 RED (SAVE/COEV-UNSTABLE + zero downloads; silent classic splice absorbing the file; no malformed guard), T4 RED via the champGame-null assertion (Round 67, R66 spec item 2, 2nd carrying — the R64 SAVE/COEV-UNSTABLE bridge converted from an honest refusal into a writer; the classic-banner-after-C1 franken tail stays OPEN, R66 spec item 1 [M])", proofTest: "tests/r67-coev-quilt-writer-glue.test.js" },
+    { id: "c1-scaling-study", claim: "the C1 scaling study tool exists and is pinned honest — tools/c1-scaling.js runs the page's OWN training loop (the tools/prerun-coev.js call sequence, parameterized) at any (population × generations × seed) arm and receipts trajectories + first5/last5 windows to research/; it is DETERMINISTIC (same arm twice = deep-equal, so a scaling difference is never weather), the probe is CONTRASTING (population size measurably changes the trajectory — pop 8 vs pop 24 at one seed diverge), and the receipt contract is DESCRIPTIVE, never a learning claim (R66's selection-noise law carried: trajectories are printed, improvement is not asserted — every summary self-labels noLearningClaim and the source carries the no-claim marker); the study never touches checkpoints/coev.js — the R45 birth seal and the canonical artifacts stay the one canonical training set (queue #2's carried C1 scaling study, bounded slice)", proofTest: "tests/c1-scaling.test.js" },
     { id: "r69-schamp-trail-glue", claim: "the C1 stats line prints d(sChamp)/d(gen) as a `sChamp trail a→b→c…` lane — a VIEW over the ledger's own receipted sFit rows (coev.ledger.tail(8)), never a separate state array that could drift; it opens at ≥2 points (one gen is a dot, not a trajectory) and crosses load boundaries because the loaded ledger re-anchors the file's rows; printed, never asserted as a learning claim (R66 P3: the trajectory is selection-noise dominated — the lane shows the spikes, it does not claim improvement) — FAIL-first on the pristine tip: T1/T2 RED (no `sChamp trail` pre-R69), T3 guards the lone-dot direction (Round 69, R68 spec item 3, 3rd carrying)", proofTest: "tests/r69-schamp-trail-glue.test.js" },
     { id: "coev-file-provenance-glue", claim: "the C1 receipts carry file provenance — receipt() accepts an optional laneGen and the row's own gen column records the C1 generation for C1-lane receipts (SAVE/COEV, SAVE/COEV-EMPTY, LOAD/COEV, LOAD/COEV-MALFORMED all pass their genC — the malformed refusal names the genC the file CLAIMED), never the classic slot (verbatim wound: load a gen-5 coev file at a fresh page — the load path never sets the classic gen — save, and the pre-R68 row silently asserted gen 0, the R56-P3-adjacent class); renderReceipts appends ` g${gen}` to /COEV-kind rows only — non-C1 rows render byte-unchanged; and the LOAD/COEV banner carries the file's NAME (f.name + genC + population sizes) so the player with three coev quilts can tell WHICH session they loaded — FAIL-first on the pristine tip: T1 RED via the render assertion (no ` g` suffix pre-R68), T2/T3/T4 RED via row.gen === 0 where 5 is claimed (Round 68, R67 spec item 4, 3rd carrying; items 1–3 of the R68 spec stay OPEN for R69)", proofTest: "tests/r68-coev-file-provenance-glue.test.js" },
     { id: "startgenc-fails-closed-glue", claim: "startGenC fails CLOSED on a half-built coev state — the guard is !coev||!coev.popS||!coev.popE, so a coev object that exists but lacks populations (a hand-built file, a future loader's partial state) materializes BOTH populations at slider size via Object.assign, preserving any existing sChamp/eChamp/genC/last/ledger; before the fix the !coev-only guard let the half-state sail through and throw TypeError at coev.popS.length INSIDE the rAF tick, killing the whole page loop (R49 P1 class; R60 fix relanded by R63 after the R61+R62 merge window closed — 7th carrying; verbatim TypeError repro'd on pristine main 9f03372 by the R63 scientist driver)", proofTest: "tests/r63-startgenc-fails-closed-glue.test.js" },
